</style></head><body class="st-body" style="background-color:#f5f5f4;padding:0"><!--$--><!--html--><!--head--><div style="display:none;overflow:hidden;line-height:1px;opacity:0;max-height:0;max-width:0" data-skip-in-text="true">Netflix went from $16.99 to $18.99<div> ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿ ‌​‍‎‏﻿</div></div><!--body--><table border="0" width="100%" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" align="center"><tbody><tr><td style="background-color:#f5f5f4;color:#1c1917;font-family:system-ui, -apple-system, &#x27;Segoe UI&#x27;, sans-serif;padding:24px 12px"><table align="center" width="100%" class="st-card" border="0" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" style="max-width:520px;background-color:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e7e5e4;border-radius:8px;padding:28px 32px"><tbody><tr style="width:100%"><td><p class="st-muted" style="font-size:13px;line-height:24px;color:#78716c;letter-spacing:1px;margin:0;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0;margin-left:0;margin-right:0">SubTracker</p><h2 style="font-size:20px;margin:14px 0 4px">Netflix<!-- --> costs more than it used to</h2><p style="font-size:15px;line-height:23px;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px">We noticed the recurring <!-- -->Netflix<!-- --> charge<!-- --> on your account ending 0042<!-- --> went from<!-- --> <strong>$16.99</strong> to<!-- --> <strong>$18.99</strong> starting 2026-05-15<!-- -->. That is all we know — the price simply changed.</p><p class="st-muted" style="font-size:14px;line-height:21px;color:#78716c;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px">If the new price still feels worth it, there is nothing to do.</p><table align="center" width="100%" border="0" cellPadding="0" cellSpacing="0" role="presentation" style="margin-top:24px"><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://app.subtracker.test/dashboard" style="color:#ffffff;text-decoration-line:none;background-color:#1c1917;border-radius:6px;display:inline-block;font-size:14px;padding:10px 18px;text-decoration:none" target="_blank">See the details</a></td></tr></tbody></table><hr class="st-hr" style="width:100%;border:none;border-top:1px solid #eaeaea;border-color:#e7e5e4;margin:28px 0 12px"/><p class="st-muted" style="font-size:12px;line-height:18px;color:#78716c;margin-top:16px;margin-bottom:16px">You are getting this because SubTracker watches your subscriptions for changes that matter. Choose which emails you get on the<!-- --> <a href="https://app.subtracker.test/settings" style="color:#2563eb;text-decoration-line:none" target="_blank">preferences page</a>. SubTracker reads transactions to help you decide — it never moves money.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></td></tr></tbody></table><!--/$--></body></html>",
  "subject": "Netflix went from $16.99 to $18.99",
}
`;

